{
  "requirement": "Marks an agent request that has begun collecting node contents. Further node inputs can be added before awaiting the answer.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct NodePhase;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.NodePhase` has two obligations. A request that has begun collecting node contents is marked by the `NodePhase` type. More node inputs can be added before the answer is awaited.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` covers both.\n\n- **Entering the phase.** The test calls `ctx.ask::<Answer>().context(..).contents_of_current_node()`. In `src/procedure.rs`, this method returns `Ask<..., NodePhase>`, so the test enters the node phase.\n- **Adding inputs in the phase.** On that phase value the test chains `.contents_of_successors(7)` and then `.contents_of_current_node()` again. The test only compiles if those methods are available on `NodePhase`. It asserts the resulting request inputs are `[1, 3, 2, 3, 1]`, with the right contents, in order and with repetition. It also asserts the recorded reads and `ctx.dependencies()`.\n- **Awaiting.** The test calls `.into_future()` and awaits the result. It asserts the answer and that the future is `Send`. Awaiting from `NodePhase` is therefore exercised.\n- **Export.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks that `NodePhase` is a public export. The requirement's `pub struct NodePhase;` declaration is covered by this check.\n\nI found no further scenario that the requirement text names and the tests miss. Other behaviors of the node phase, such as ordering and the rendering of inputs, belong to the `judge.*` requirements. The same test also carries `{test}` references to those requirements.",
  "references": "537a3b787fdbb0ee52c8060f2a798a5226ba0f61f1a6005ac3d1d8b63fef67fa",
